            in the case of K-dimensional loss. `input` is expected to be log-probabilities.
        target: :math:`(N)` where each value is :math:`0 \leq \text{targets}[i] \leq C-1`,
            or :math:`(N, d_1, d_2, ..., d_K)` where :math:`K \geq 1` for
            K-dimensional loss.
